WEBVTT

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.520
It's been a long time since we laid
on the ground together like this, Mel.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.350
You're right.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.150
-I wish we could stay like this forever.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.360
Me too.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.120
You're going to the Capital, Rin?

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.700
Then you've got to get going.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.500
What about you, Mel?

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.040
I can't go.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.630
You know that, right?

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.090
Keep singing, okay?

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.350
I'm sure there are people waiting
to hear your songs.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.430
People waiting to hear my songs?

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.820
<i>You guys run away!</i>

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.200
I'm the one those guys are after!

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.030
Those guys?

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.990
-What do you mean?
<i>-Rin!</i>

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.240
Rin!

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.830
That man... He's... that guy from before.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.340
Wait. Wait!

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:12.060
THE SONG OF ENCOUNTER

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:17.900
What a masterpiece.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.530
If the Court Orchestra had performed,

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.910
we could have made the power
of the songs even stronger.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.200
True. Though...

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.170
how did you manage to convince
that pacifist of a songstress?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.550
Controlling a woman who has
ridiculous feelings for someone is easy.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.050
Excuse me.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.640
Miss Finis has suppressed the enemy.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.640
We can now march
to the Mont Valay fortress.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.220
That was so fast.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.310
Good job.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.020
However...

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.480
Miss Finis!

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.780
The God of Destruction!
The Goddess of Victory!

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.160
Miss Finis!

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.370
There's a reason you're doing this,
isn't there?

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.330
Otherwise, there's no reason
to risk your life

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.340
doing something like this.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.340
What happened?

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:28.890
Henry.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.160
Sorry for overworking you.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.370
Hang in there just a little bit longer.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.080
Finis.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.920
I guess our carriage couldn't catch up
to a Capital Army's horse.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.640
I'm too beautiful to camp outside.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.470
The checkpoint is nearby,
so there aren't any bandits around.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.390
We'll be fine.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.190
What I hate are the bugs! Bugs!

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.520
Buzz, buzz, buzz.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.770
Stop that!

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:22.690
-Scary!
-Good job, Monica.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.200
Hey, Rin.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.280
Do you know the knight we saw?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.290
Well, not exactly.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.420
The Leobolt family is
a distinguished family in the Capital.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.500
It's a mystery that you know each other.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.170
And it's also a mystery why he was alone.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.140
Now, can you tell me...

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.470
the real reason you want to go
to the Capital.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:00.480
Allow me to explain.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.370
I see.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.120
That must have been really hard.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.880
Rin is really amazing.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.920
She's already started to move forward.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.550
You're right.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.050
And Al--

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.470
She learned the Song
of the Four Great Spirits from you,

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:35.140
-to use her power to help others--
-You too, Al.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:39.890
It must have been hard for you, too.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.610
I...

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:49.070
Right! I have to go look for materials
for my inventions!

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.070
Please get some rest.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.030
Scientists don't need sleep!

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.450
Okay.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:57.250
I'm going to bed now.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.750
Take as much time as you need.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:39.120
Look who's here. What are you doing
at a place like this, Mr. Leobolt?

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:40.580
Don't play dumb.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:45.170
Are you talking about that Weapon
who passed through?

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.040
Don't call her a Weapon!

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.340
She was a symbol of peace.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.010
Peace will not return
unless we win the war.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:59.470
And we follow the orders of General Bazra.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:01.100
General Bazra?

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:04.060
You understand
what I'm trying to say, right?

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.230
Orders that come from a general
in the Capital Army

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.990
are equivalent to orders from the prince
and direct orders from the king.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.530
So, that's the western checkpoint?

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.910
Think they'll let us through?

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:24.120
The Capital Army isn't that nice.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:28.630
No. If they catch us, I'll...

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.760
You're going to sleep here?

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:33.840
Hey! It's that man again!

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:36.340
You're right!

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.850
They might let us through
if we say we're friends

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:41.970
-with that knight!
-Wait.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.190
They're arguing about something.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.480
General Bazra?!

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.270
You can't let a man like him
lead the war!

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.400
You should be careful what you say.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.860
Criticizing the general or the Capital
is a serious crime.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.070
What did you say?!

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.160
Guards! Capture him!

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:06.370
-They're fighting each other.
-This is our chance!

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.960
-We've got to bet on this!
-What are you going to do?

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.420
We'll take advantage of the commotion.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.130
But... That man...

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.720
If we get caught, it's over.
We have to pass the checkpoint.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:19.930
Here we go.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.390
What's going on?!

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.980
We can't let rebels like you get away.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:29.900
If you interfere with the war,
you're an enemy.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.940
-I never interfered--
-He's dangerous! Capture him!

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.580
There's someone I have to save.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:45.000
If you interfere, I won't go easy on you.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.750
Don't lose your composure!
Kill him if you have to!

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.010
He's so strong!

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.720
We can't get close!

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:03.510
What are you doing?

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.350
Go! Get him! All of you!

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:09.600
What?!

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.480
Will we make it?!

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:16.740
-Wait! Who are you?!
-Women and children. Ignore them.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:21.410
You're--

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.580
Now! Archers!

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:34.300
<i>The name of the wind</i>

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:38.470
<i>The name of the wind</i>

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.800
<i>If you call</i>

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:46.640
<i>The wind will answer</i>

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.560
Could it be?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.310
Can you use the power of songs, too?

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:55.270
Stop the singing girl!
Don't let her through!

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.940
Close the other door!

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:01.200
Come on!

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:02.320
You!

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.580
-Get away!
-Let me go, you idiot!

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.830
-Ow, ow, ow!
-What is this thing?

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:15.840
Good work! Throw them all in prison!

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.410
<i>What are you saying?!</i>

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:49.250
He'll execute Henry
if you don't attack the enemy

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.330
with the power of your songs?

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.420
<i>How horrible!</i>

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.170
I didn't want to sing.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.220
I didn't want...

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.220
to sing at all!

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:08.760
But still, I...

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.270
You must...

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.310
care about him a lot.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:19.780
If I lost Henry...

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:23.900
I...

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:27.530
It'll be okay. It'll be okay.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:30.740
I--

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.000
<i>I'll do something about it.</i>

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:05.030
The Leobolt family sword is said
to be the strongest

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.700
on the entire continent.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:10.990
It's made from minerals that never rust.
That's amazing.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:16.080
Be careful. It'll cut your body in two
in an instant.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.210
Shut up!

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:20.500
You're just a rich kid. Don't be so cocky!

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:31.810
Most of you guys are just kids.
But you look like a good woman.

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:33.930
Let's have some fun.

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:38.020
Hey, loser, if you don't want me
snapping your head off,

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.020
bring me a blanket and go away.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.320
What?!

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:43.610
And a big barrel of ale.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:44.530
You--

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:47.450
Looks like I need to teach you
some manners.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:48.360
Hey.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.490
Don't you dare touch them.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:55.540
Or else I'll do whatever it takes
to snap your head off.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:58.710
What's wrong with you guys?
Snapping my head off?

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:01.540
An unarmed knight like you
can't do anything--

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:04.050
Don't underestimate me.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:07.470
Even without a sword,
I can take your life.

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.590
I got it! I got it! Stop!

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:17.560
Damn! It hurts!

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.520
Allow me to apologize for his rudeness.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:24.190
I'm sorry.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:29.490
He's got good looks, a nice personality
and skills.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.450
Guys like that are my favorite.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:34.990
Favorite? Are you talking about food?

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.620
Even at a time like this...

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.420
You said it.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.000
Good morning.

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.340
This is chaos.

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.760
Food!

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:05.570
<i>I see.</i>

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:08.780
You healed my wounds

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:12.070
with the power of your songs when we met.

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:16.660
Damn!

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:20.040
The Capital Army saw it.
That's why your village was--

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:21.960
It's my fault.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:24.040
But...

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.800
why is the Capital Army after you,
a knight from the Capital?

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:34.010
The Leobolt family has always
pledged loyalty to the Capital.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:38.430
But I oppose what the Capital Army
is doing right now.

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:42.690
They use their military to oppress.
The royal family is corrupt.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:45.650
Yeah. They're rotten to the core.

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:49.900
That's why I'm going around
to gather the opposition.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:53.740
I was planning to advise the Capital
to change their ways.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:55.620
I see.

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.990
The Minstrel Hunt was conducted...

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.910
just to capture Rin.

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:04.290
No way!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.630
Why does the Capital Army want
to capture Rin?

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:10.010
For the power of her songs.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:13.470
The power of my songs?

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:17.470
The Capital Army is trying to use

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.350
the power of songs as a weapon for war.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.400
Miss Finis.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:33.820
Excuse me.

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:38.620
Miss Finis...

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.540
Um... Where is Miss Finis?

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:46.460
She wasn't feeling well
and went to draw some water.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:47.630
By herself?

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:49.920
Yeah. The watering hole is close by.

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:53.050
Hey! It's that way!

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.380
That's why I'm going the opposite way!

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.140
Where is the water?

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:04.640
Corte.

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:06.600
Henry.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.940
I'm a Weapon of Song?

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.190
Yeah.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:14.110
But I'm indebted to you.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.110
I'll protect you.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.240
And...

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.200
I'm going to save her, too.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.960
-I'm happy.
-This has nothing to do with you.

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:28.040
"Her"?

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:31.880
There's another woman
who possesses the power of songs.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:35.670
There's someone else with the power?

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:41.510
This war began because the Armies started
a struggle over the power of songs.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.390
That woman is already being misused...

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:48.060
as a Human Weapon by the Capital Army.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:49.650
No way.

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:51.520
That's terrible!

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:55.190
I'm sure she must also love singing.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:57.490
Rin.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:00.120
In any case, let's escape.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.910
They're trying to use you
to do bad things.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:05.830
I can't get out.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:10.500
-Good job, you hottie!
-His looks don't matter.

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:20.680
Thanks.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:23.720
If I hadn't been defeated
by them back there,

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:27.480
you wouldn't have had to lose your family
and village.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.440
Bring out the girl who sings!

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.520
Kill the rest of them.

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:34.780
Got it!

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:35.940
Here we go!

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:37.360
They're coming!

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:39.570
Rin! We have to hurry!

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:42.280
Al, cause a disturbance
with your Star Bombs.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.700
Allu, Monica, are you ready to run?

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:45.790
Yeah.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:47.870
What's going on in there?!

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:03.930
Where did that rich kid go?

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:07.310
He went off on his own to the front line.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:10.270
I bet he's been captured by now.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:11.940
What did you say?

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:17.280
What?!

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:18.690
The songstress.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.200
Where are we?

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.120
<i>It's not your fault, Leobolt.</i>

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:26.620
The Capital Army is to blame.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:28.370
But...

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.170
when the war's over,
could you come to my village...

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:36.800
to meet Mel, Grandpa...

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:39.510
and everyone else?

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:41.760
They escaped!

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:44.340
There! The carriage is over there!

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:49.350
I'll definitely go... to pay my respects.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.230
You. Why are you in a place like this?

00:19:55.310 --> 00:19:58.780
Henry... Where's Henry?!

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:03.780
Take that!

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:09.330
Wait! Monica's not here!

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:11.210
She's over there!

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.170
Are you serious?!

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:16.630
Don't sleep over there!

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:21.510
There you are, you brat!

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:23.840
-Die!
-Monica!

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:33.140
-He-- He flew!
-It's the Song of Wind.

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:35.600
-Let's go! Run!
-Yeah!

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:41.530
Stop them! Stop them now!

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:50.830
Rin!

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.170
-Go, before the gate closes!
-But--

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:59.670
If you head west,
you'll reach Dr. Weissen's laboratory.

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:01.380
You'll be safe there.

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.590
Dr. Weissen?!

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:04.680
Wait!

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:08.050
Hurry! I'll hold them back!

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:08.970
Here we go!

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:11.970
Wait!

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:14.730
What's the name of the songstress?

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.650
It's Finis!

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:22.900
Finis?

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:28.700
It's no use! We won't make it!

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:32.330
Damn! We're shut in!

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:37.790
Now you're going to become
a Human Weapon, too!

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:40.920
I'm not going to become... a Weapon!

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:46.510
<i>Let the wind rage</i>
<i>After the wind rages</i>

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:50.180
<i>The light will shine in the sky</i>

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:53.810
You can't blow down the gate
with a wind like that!

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:57.100
<i>Arise</i>
<i>Our hope</i>

00:21:57.640 --> 00:22:02.570
<i>Let the wind rage</i>
<i>After the wind rages</i>

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:07.240
<i>The light will shine in the sky</i>

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:09.570
We're flying!

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:13.830
<i>The wind sweeps everything away</i>

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:19.210
<i>Because it is the wind</i>
